        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0672" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg548"/>

                <head>No. 334.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Hoppin</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 8,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 257.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 248, of the
                    20th ultimo, to you, relative to the delivery of the papers of American ships
                    into the custody of the customs authorities on the west coast of Africa, I now
                    have to inclose herewith, for your information, a copy of a letter dated the
                    24th ultimo, from Messrs. Yates &amp; Porterfield, explaining their letter of
                    the 18th of the same month, on the subject in question.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to make such further communication to Her Majesty’s Government
                    on the subject as the tenor of your former note may in your judgment,
                    require.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d338-a1.xml" xpointer="d338-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
